Project Overview 
Project Title: Personalized Learning Roadmap

Category: Software / AI Workflow
Problem

High-quality free technical learning content exists in abundance (e.g. roadmap.humblebee.ai), yet completion rates remain extremely low. The root cause is a one-size-fits-all path:

Experienced learners get bored by material they already know and quit.
Beginners hit advanced sections without prerequisites and quit out of overwhelm.
There is no verification of understanding, so learners advance on the illusion of progress.

This destroys completion, retention, and any claim of effectiveness for learning platforms, corporate L&D teams, and education providers.
Target Users / Buyers (we keep all three open)

Learning platforms / content publishers that suffer from high drop-off.
Companies running internal technical upskilling programs with staff of widely different starting points.
Education providers offering supplementary material to students with uneven backgrounds.

Proposed Solution

An AI-powered system that:

Assesses a learner’s current level and goal from open-ended answers.
Generates a personalized ordered path through the real roadmap.humblebee.ai content, explicitly marking and justifying skipped sections.
Creates checkpoint questions and coding problems from the actual content.
Blocks or adapts the path based on checkpoint performance.
Produces visibly different paths for different learner profiles.

Why AI is necessary

Fixed decision trees cannot:

Interpret open-ended experience descriptions.
Generate paths for arbitrary goals.
Create high-quality checkpoints at scale from real content.



